+## 1. Result and activation boundary
+
+H2 mounts `/host/pocketrisu/v1/*` behind mandatory bearer authentication and
+joins the process-memory execution context to the durable execution claim and
+HostPrepare row. Existing `/prepare-turn`, `/complete-turn`,
+`/proxy/plugin-main`, and synchronous Source Discovery consumers accept the
+host reference only after the same authenticated owner, claim epoch, prepare
+fingerprint, context ID, settings digest, stage, and host-change watermarks
+match.
+
+Main, supervisor, critic, embedding, source-search, prepare, complete, and
+preprocessing callers use the captured context. Context-aware branches do not
+read current runtime config, environment fallbacks, preprocessing settings, or
+prompt files. A request with no host reference continues through the existing
+legacy branch.
+
+This is not product activation:
+
+- `production_consumer_version` remains `0`;
+- `product_activation` remains `false`;
+- no PocketRisu JavaScript caller or capability was changed;
+- no live Archive Center or PocketRisu process, data, provider, tag, release,
+  or upstream remote was changed.
+
+## 2. Runtime audit phase 1 — flat discovery
+
+The following list is intentionally severity-free.
+
+- The route group adds capability, execution acquire, context capture,
+  prepare start/status/complete/fail/unknown/skip, and execution settle calls.
+- Every host route runs through a mandatory bearer-token comparison even when
+  global authentication enforcement is disabled.
+- Host JSON accepts only `application/json`, rejects unknown fields and
+  trailing documents, and caps request bodies at 2 MiB.
+- Capability reporting now requires execution, prepare, durable-key recovery,
+  restart scan, and in-memory context owners.
+- Capture rereads the active execution claim and exact owner identity.
+- Capture freezes the device allowlist, RuntimeConfig, environment-derived
+  embedding fallback, preprocessing settings, supervisor prompt, and critic
+  prompt under the configuration lock.
+- Capture registers context ID and public digest with HostPrepare.
+- Same-process exact capture replay returns the existing context and prepare.
+- Changed device material under one operation returns conflict.
+- Lost capture response plus process restart recovers the durable prepare by
+  stable key and returns the old context ID/digest as
+  `settings_context_unavailable` without allocating a replacement context.
+- Prepare start retains the existing single CAS authorization and run epoch.
+- Prepare completion accepts only a strict `pocketrisu_prepare_result.v1`
+  envelope whose owner fields and compact assembled-payload SHA-256 match.
+- Prepared-result publication rejects captured credentials, endpoint values,
+  override values, preprocessing prompts, and system prompts.
+- Status can report captured, released, or restart-missing context state.
+- Known failure and outcome-unknown remain durable non-replay states.
+- Explicit unavailable skip can release the exact claim even after context
+  memory was lost.
+- Execution settle releases secret-bearing material and preserves a bounded
+  terminal tombstone for exact replay.
+- Startup scans running prepares in bounded batches and converts unprovable
+  external outcomes to `outcome_unknown` before readiness.
+- Active context count and encoded bytes retain the existing 64-entry/16 MiB
+  fail-closed ceiling; released tombstones are capped at 256.
+- Internal prompt writes now share the same configuration lock as capture.
+- Prepare settings are replaced by the captured allowlist, including input
+  context, memory budgets, narrative stance, and top-k values.
+- The server-host prepare observation binds raw input SHA-256, input receipt,
+  source revision, semantic pre-injection hash, operation owner, claim epoch,
+  and required host-change sequence.
+- Consumer admission rejects a stale claim, wrong stage, cross-owner
+  reference, changed digest, or unsafe required/ingested host-change prefix.
+- Vector query embedding uses the captured embedding provider.
+- Preprocessing uses captured role settings and captured supervisor fallback.
+- Supervisor uses the captured provider and captured system-prompt bytes.
+- Main proxy replaces request-supplied provider settings with the captured
+  main config, preserves custom endpoint/override behavior, and rejects the
+  connection-test branch.
+- Complete uses the captured critic, embedding, prompt, intervals, and
+  redaction values.
+- Complete source acceptance v4 binds the server commit receipt/revision to the
+  same host, operation, prepare, context, input receipt, and content hashes.
+- A context-aware complete replay can return the exact in-process idempotency
+  response after context release without rerunning provider or persistence.
+- Synchronous Source Discovery create/resume uses captured critic and search
+  settings; detaching a context into the asynchronous corpus-analysis job is
+  rejected.
+- Context-aware provider errors redact captured API keys, full endpoints,
+  endpoint query values, and JSON override values.
+- Context-aware preprocessing response traces remove system prompts, provider
+  model input, raw provider output, input maps, endpoint hosts, and
+  content-derived prompt metadata.
+- Legacy requests without `pocketrisu_host_context` retain their previous
+  settings, prompt reads, source acceptance v1-v3, custom endpoint, Ollama,
+  and environment fallback paths.
+- The implementation adds no background loop, listener, client capability,
+  JavaScript mutation, or paid-provider test call.
