+# PocketRisu host session execution C0 validation
+
+Date: 2026-09-13 KST
+
+Status: **store primitive validated; product host route and integration remain
+unimplemented**
+
+## Scope and authority
+
+This is the C0-B experiment for the PocketRisu server chat-save integration
+plan. It starts from Archive Center `026dcbf3b45adcf69b254673d439b24e943115b3`
+and records implementation commit `2b16b56`. It adds only:
+
+- an additive MariaDB execution slot and terminal-outcome migration;
+- an optional MariaDB store interface for acquire, status, and settle;
+- route-binding epoch derivation;
+- source, SQL-mock, and explicitly disposable MariaDB tests; and
+- session-migration metadata exclusions.
+
+No HTTP route, capability advertisement, Archive Center JavaScript change,
+PocketRisu change, provider call, or production installation is part of this
+slice.
+
+## Runtime audit Phase 1 — flat discovery
+
+- Migration 014 creates one active execution slot per canonical session.
+- Migration 014 creates immutable terminal outcomes keyed by host/operation and
+  host/end-event identities.
+- Migration 014 preserves the requested terminal reason separately from the
+  final reason selected after a route fence.
+- The content-copy session migration manifest remains v4 and classifies both
+  new tables as coordination metadata exclusions.
+- A route-binding epoch hashes the complete durable route identity, revision,
+  and creation instant.
+- Acquire validates every identity and the expected binding epoch.
+- Acquire returns an existing terminal result before treating a later route
+  revision as a new operation.
+- Acquire serializes the route and session slot in a MariaDB transaction.
+- Acquire returns the same claim for an identical active operation.
+- Acquire returns wait for another active operation in the same canonical
+  session, including operations submitted through different host bindings.
+- Acquire blocks when the recorded safe host-change boundary is behind the
+  required boundary.
+- Acquire increments claim epoch with a compare-and-set update and rejects
+  integer exhaustion.
+- MariaDB deadlock and lock-timeout errors retry the complete immutable
+  transaction within a fixed bound.
+- Status reads terminal outcomes before active slots and compares active slots
+  with the current route binding.
+- Settle requires the exact host, route, operation, binding epoch, claim epoch,
+  end event, requested reason, and source disposition fingerprint.
+- Settle stores the terminal outcome and releases the exact active slot in one
+  transaction.
+- A route change converts the final terminal reason to `binding_changed` while
+  retaining the requested reason.
+- A stale or repeated settle cannot clear a newer claim.
+- Terminal outcomes and session slots have no compaction or retention policy in
+  this slice.
+- The slot has only one required/ingested/safe sequence snapshot; per-binding
+  host-change streams do not exist in this slice.
+- Only `claimed` and terminal phases exist; previous-turn
+  `awaiting_next_input` does not exist in this slice.
+- Outcomes do not yet reference prepare keys, settings contexts, input
+  receipts, or commit receipts.
+- The optional store interface has no production caller and is not mounted as
+  an HTTP route.
+- The additive migration is loaded by the existing ordered production schema
+  tool.
+- Identifier data is parameterized SQL input; raw chat or model content is not
+  stored by these tables.
+- Retry uses bounded timers and adds no worker, background loop, socket, or
+  external lock service.
